1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,457
There was a time a farm got
found by the sign on the road.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,715
Today it gets found on
a phone. In a kitchen.

3
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:08,985
Before anyone picks up the car keys.

4
00:00:09,283 --> 00:00:11,195
Here's a number that should worry you.

5
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:15,620
A national survey asked US farms that
welcome visitors how they market.

6
00:00:15,801 --> 00:00:18,442
The big two were social
media and word of mouth.

7
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:22,814
No other marketing tool was
used by even half of them.

8
00:00:23,117 --> 00:00:26,356
So if you want to get your
farm on Google Maps, for free,

9
00:00:26,376 --> 00:00:27,755
this video is for you.

10
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:30,889
Without paying for ads. Without a website.

11
00:00:30,978 --> 00:00:32,973
And without being good with computers.

12
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,938
Maybe there's a quiet voice saying,

13
00:00:34,958 --> 00:00:37,055
"Who would ever look
for a farm like mine?"

14
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:39,482
Somebody already is.

15
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:43,599
In this video, we will see why
good farms go invisible online,

16
00:00:43,619 --> 00:00:46,305
visit a family dairy that
learned it the hard way,

17
00:00:46,325 --> 00:00:48,563
and walk through the
free fix in three steps.

18
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:50,194
Stay for number three.

19
00:00:50,268 --> 00:00:52,037
It's the step most farmers skip,

20
00:00:52,057 --> 00:00:53,593
and it's where the visitors are.

21
00:00:53,883 --> 00:00:56,574
I'm Sarah. Yes, I'm a cartoon.

22
00:00:56,694 --> 00:00:58,521
This channel comes from Stephen Loke,

23
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:01,939
whose farm is featured in
Bloomberg News and Asahi Shimbun.

24
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:06,726
Here's the enemy. It isn't
you. You're farming right.

25
00:01:07,017 --> 00:01:09,027
The enemy is being invisible.

26
00:01:09,317 --> 00:01:12,394
Picture a family planning
their Saturday. They type,

27
00:01:12,414 --> 00:01:14,965
pick your own near me. Up comes a map.

28
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:19,329
Some farms show smiling faces,
opening hours, a phone number.

29
00:01:19,402 --> 00:01:23,064
Then there's a gray pin.
No photos. No hours.

30
00:01:23,191 --> 00:01:25,681
Maybe a name somebody
else typed in years ago.

31
00:01:25,983 --> 00:01:27,951
Which one would you drive an hour for?

32
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:30,365
That's the ghost pin.

33
00:01:30,526 --> 00:01:31,770
And the hard part is,

34
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:34,242
many farm owners don't
even know it's there.

35
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:37,278
So here's the big idea
I want you to remember.

36
00:01:37,405 --> 00:01:38,938
Your farm has two gates.

37
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:40,984
The first gate is on your road.

38
00:01:41,088 --> 00:01:42,795
You open it every morning.

39
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:44,695
The second gate is on a phone,

40
00:01:44,715 --> 00:01:46,503
in a kitchen forty miles away.

41
00:01:46,611 --> 00:01:48,946
That's where people decide
whether to come at all.

42
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:52,817
Most farmers open the first gate
and leave the second one locked.

43
00:01:53,117 --> 00:01:54,499
Call it the Second Gate.

44
00:01:54,671 --> 00:01:56,156
And opening it is free.

45
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:59,378
Google says its local
results rest on three things.

46
00:01:59,575 --> 00:02:01,265
How well you match the search.

47
00:02:01,404 --> 00:02:02,693
How far away you are.

48
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:04,251
And how well known you are.

49
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:05,936
You can't move your farm.

50
00:02:06,087 --> 00:02:08,031
But the other two are in your hands.

51
00:02:09,217 --> 00:02:10,863
Fairbury, Illinois.

52
00:02:10,949 --> 00:02:12,294
Nineteen fifty-eight.

53
00:02:12,405 --> 00:02:14,553
Duane and Arlene Kilgus start a dairy.

54
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:16,247
For more than thirty years,

55
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:19,862
they sell their milk the way
most farmers do. To a co-op.

56
00:02:20,012 --> 00:02:21,376
At the co-op's price.

57
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:24,177
But the family wanted more
than the co-op's price.

58
00:02:24,358 --> 00:02:26,268
Therefore they did something bold.

59
00:02:26,417 --> 00:02:29,734
They started bottling their own
Jersey milk, right on the farm.

60
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:31,400
They sold it to stores,

61
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,967
restaurants and coffee
shops up in Chicago.

62
00:02:34,152 --> 00:02:35,516
And in twenty oh nine,

63
00:02:35,536 --> 00:02:37,788
they opened a little
country store on the farm,

64
00:02:37,808 --> 00:02:39,173
a mile south of town.

65
00:02:40,283 --> 00:02:42,158
Then came spring twenty twenty.

66
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:43,827
The restaurants closed.

67
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,948
The family supplied about
two dozen of them in Chicago.

68
00:02:47,025 --> 00:02:50,659
And most of those customers shut
their doors, at least for a while.

69
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:52,637
Therefore the family cut the herd,

70
00:02:52,657 --> 00:02:56,844
from about a hundred and fifty cows
to a hundred and fifteen. And still,

71
00:02:56,864 --> 00:03:00,345
it wasn't enough. Some of the milk
had to be dumped in the field.

72
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:04,262
Picture it. Fresh milk
from cows you raised.

73
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:05,764
Poured onto the grass.

74
00:03:06,850 --> 00:03:08,928
But one part of the farm kept going.

75
00:03:09,026 --> 00:03:10,451
That little country store.

76
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:13,705
During the pandemic, more
people came through its door.

77
00:03:13,811 --> 00:03:16,399
And a steady crowd of
customers still comes today.

78
00:03:16,683 --> 00:03:19,431
Why? Because people knew
where that gate was.

79
00:03:19,626 --> 00:03:21,095
When the trucks stopped coming,

80
00:03:21,115 --> 00:03:23,928
the customers who could
find the farm kept coming.

81
00:03:24,217 --> 00:03:27,723
Here's the lesson. You don't get
found in the middle of a crisis.

82
00:03:27,904 --> 00:03:29,391
You get found before it.

83
00:03:29,683 --> 00:03:31,927
If you're thinking about
welcoming visitors,

84
00:03:31,947 --> 00:03:35,461
Stephen wrote a free checklist called
the Twenty-One Point Blueprint.

85
00:03:35,613 --> 00:03:38,627
Everything to have in place
before your first paying guest.

86
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:40,501
The link is in the description.

87
00:03:40,629 --> 00:03:42,029
More about it at the end.

88
00:03:42,317 --> 00:03:44,576
And if this is helping, subscribe,

89
00:03:44,596 --> 00:03:46,481
so the next farm lesson finds you.

90
00:03:47,683 --> 00:03:49,421
Now, what this is not.

91
00:03:49,584 --> 00:03:50,986
This isn't paid ads.

92
00:03:51,157 --> 00:03:52,954
It isn't dancing on TikTok.

93
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:56,625
And it isn't a marketing agency
sending you a bill every month.

94
00:03:56,917 --> 00:04:01,147
In fact, Google says you can't pay for
a better spot in its local results.

95
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:04,252
The spot is earned. And the
tool to earn it is free.

96
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:08,999
It's called a Google Business Profile.
Here's the fix, in three steps.

97
00:04:10,183 --> 00:04:12,518
Step number one. Find your pin.

98
00:04:12,817 --> 00:04:15,493
Take out your phone. Open Google Maps.

99
00:04:15,595 --> 00:04:16,840
Type your farm's name,

100
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:18,124
the one on your sign.

101
00:04:18,417 --> 00:04:20,415
Now look. Is there a pin?

102
00:04:20,505 --> 00:04:23,415
Is it in the right place?
Are the hours right?

103
00:04:23,531 --> 00:04:25,176
Is that even your phone number?

104
00:04:25,483 --> 00:04:28,451
Sometimes Google already
has a listing for your farm,

105
00:04:28,471 --> 00:04:30,068
built from what it found online,

106
00:04:30,088 --> 00:04:31,992
or one a visitor suggested.

107
00:04:32,177 --> 00:04:34,341
You might be on the map
and not even know it.

108
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:37,128
If there's no pin at all, that's fine too.

109
00:04:37,242 --> 00:04:39,098
You'll make one in step number two.

110
00:04:40,283 --> 00:04:42,375
Step number two. Claim it,

111
00:04:42,395 --> 00:04:43,691
and prove it's yours.

112
00:04:43,983 --> 00:04:46,078
Go to business dot google dot com.

113
00:04:46,192 --> 00:04:47,954
Sign in with a Google account.

114
00:04:48,082 --> 00:04:50,294
Search for your farm, and claim it.

115
00:04:50,381 --> 00:04:51,617
If there's no listing,

116
00:04:51,636 --> 00:04:53,495
add your farm as a new business.

117
00:04:53,783 --> 00:04:56,167
It costs nothing. Not a cent.

118
00:04:56,450 --> 00:04:58,626
Then Google asks you to
prove you're the owner.

119
00:04:58,822 --> 00:05:03,983
It may offer a phone call, a text, an
email, or a short video. For a video,

120
00:05:04,003 --> 00:05:06,014
you film your sign, your farm,

121
00:05:06,034 --> 00:05:07,761
and something only the owner has,

122
00:05:07,781 --> 00:05:10,115
like the key to your
store or your farm tools.

123
00:05:10,256 --> 00:05:12,044
Just follow the steps it gives you.

124
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:15,056
One warning. Use your farm's real name.

125
00:05:15,204 --> 00:05:16,468
The one on your sign.

126
00:05:16,564 --> 00:05:19,677
Google's rules say extra keywords
don't belong in the name,

127
00:05:19,697 --> 00:05:22,365
and adding them can get
your listing suspended.

128
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:24,843
Step number three.

129
00:05:24,987 --> 00:05:26,700
The one I told you to stay for.

130
00:05:26,845 --> 00:05:28,132
Fill every box.

131
00:05:28,417 --> 00:05:32,488
This is the step most farmers skip.
They claim the listing, feel good,

132
00:05:32,508 --> 00:05:35,266
and walk away. And the pin stays a ghost.

133
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:37,589
Google says when a profile is complete,

134
00:05:37,609 --> 00:05:42,041
people are two point seven times more
likely to see the business as reputable.

135
00:05:42,228 --> 00:05:44,612
And seventy percent more likely to visit.

136
00:05:44,917 --> 00:05:46,466
So here's what to fill in.

137
00:05:46,647 --> 00:05:47,959
Your main category.

138
00:05:48,087 --> 00:05:49,825
Choose what visitors come to do,

139
00:05:49,845 --> 00:05:53,213
not only what you grow. Type
something like, pick your own,

140
00:05:53,233 --> 00:05:54,934
and see what Google suggests.

141
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:58,389
Your real hours. If
you're seasonal, say so.

142
00:05:58,524 --> 00:06:00,080
Mark the days you're closed.

143
00:06:00,383 --> 00:06:02,192
Photos of people having fun.

144
00:06:02,331 --> 00:06:03,704
Kids feeding the goats.

145
00:06:03,779 --> 00:06:05,721
A family at the picnic table.

146
00:06:05,872 --> 00:06:07,218
Not just your crops.

147
00:06:07,517 --> 00:06:09,375
Your phone number and how to book.

148
00:06:09,472 --> 00:06:12,760
And a few plain sentences
about what a visit feels like.

149
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:18,415
That's the Second Gate, unlocked.
Same farm. Same road. But now,

150
00:06:18,435 --> 00:06:20,420
when that family in the kitchen searches,

151
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,269
your farm shows up with a face.

152
00:06:23,483 --> 00:06:25,329
Maybe you're thinking, "Sarah,

153
00:06:25,349 --> 00:06:27,558
my farm is too remote for any of this."

154
00:06:27,850 --> 00:06:31,110
Here's the truth. Remote
is exactly why you need it.

155
00:06:31,417 --> 00:06:34,297
Nobody drives past a
remote farm by accident.

156
00:06:34,395 --> 00:06:36,790
Every single visitor
will look you up first.

157
00:06:36,857 --> 00:06:38,422
If the Second Gate is locked,

158
00:06:38,442 --> 00:06:40,866
the trip ends right there, in the kitchen.

159
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:43,915
And if you're thinking, "I'm
no good with computers,"

160
00:06:43,935 --> 00:06:48,629
USDA figures show eighty-two percent
of American farms have a smartphone.

161
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:52,081
If you can send a photo to your
grandkids, you can do this.

162
00:06:53,283 --> 00:06:56,272
Remember that sign on the
road? It still matters.

163
00:06:56,408 --> 00:06:58,315
But today it's only the first gate.

164
00:06:58,617 --> 00:07:02,542
The Kilgus family's store kept going
because people knew where to find it.

165
00:07:02,684 --> 00:07:04,366
Your farm deserves the same.

166
00:07:05,450 --> 00:07:08,393
Watching this won't change
anything. Doing will.

167
00:07:08,683 --> 00:07:10,907
So here's your homework. Today,

168
00:07:10,927 --> 00:07:13,118
search your farm's name on Google Maps.

169
00:07:13,217 --> 00:07:17,606
Then tell me in the comments what
you found. Nothing? A ghost pin?

170
00:07:17,790 --> 00:07:18,994
Or a full listing?

171
00:07:19,283 --> 00:07:21,397
And if you're getting
ready to welcome visitors,

172
00:07:21,417 --> 00:07:24,067
grab Stephen's free
Twenty-One Point Blueprint.

173
00:07:24,383 --> 00:07:28,723
Why is it free? Because it's the checklist
Stephen wishes he'd had when he started,

174
00:07:28,743 --> 00:07:32,236
and he'd rather you get the basics
right before your first paying guest.

175
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,002
Inside are twenty-one
points in five phases.

176
00:07:35,109 --> 00:07:39,660
Protecting your farm: zoning,
insurance, your neighbors, your money.

177
00:07:39,725 --> 00:07:42,348
Your offer and your price. Safe parking,

178
00:07:42,368 --> 00:07:44,175
clean toilets and clear signs.

179
00:07:44,325 --> 00:07:46,413
Your booking system, your website,

180
00:07:46,433 --> 00:07:47,893
and your Google profile.

181
00:07:47,999 --> 00:07:49,427
That's point seventeen.

182
00:07:49,558 --> 00:07:52,459
And a friends and family
test run before you open.

183
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:54,453
Print it out, grab a pen,

184
00:07:54,473 --> 00:07:55,938
and walk your land with it.

185
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,816
Click the link in the description,

186
00:07:57,836 --> 00:08:00,346
enter your name and email, and it's yours.

187
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:03,563
And for ideas on what to
offer once people find you,

188
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:05,222
there's Stephen's free ebook too,

189
00:08:05,242 --> 00:08:08,823
One Hundred Fifty Ways to Unlock
Hidden Wealth From Your Farm.

190
00:08:08,987 --> 00:08:11,227
That link is in the description as well.

191
00:08:11,517 --> 00:08:14,971
Next, watch Fifty Ways to
Make Extra Money on Your Farm,

192
00:08:14,991 --> 00:08:16,538
Ranked by Startup Cost.

193
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:19,451
It shows what to offer once
people start finding you.

194
00:08:20,517 --> 00:08:22,542
Two gates. Open both.

